// TEST: a generic doubling called with a struct (rejects)
// ============================================================================
// The numbers-only rule (formalism 2.4; the user's ruling of 2026-11-14): a
// generic body's arithmetic needs a NUMBER at every instance, judged at the
// call (GONumericOperand) or, for an instance with no element class, after
// monomorphization (IRValidate check 1d). On master 1e6a871a this died in g++
// (BL9002). A struct has no element class, so the post-monomorphization
// backstop refuses the instance.
// ============================================================================
struct P {
    a: Float64
}
function dbl(x) = x + x
let a = dbl(1)
let q = dbl(P { a = 1.0 })
// ERROR: BL3001
